I added `src/pricing.test.ts` with 10 tests for `orderTotal`. They pass, and the mutation check caught every planted bug.

- **Tests:** `npx vitest run` gives 10 passed, 0 failed.
- **Scan:** `canfail scan` reported no fake-test patterns.
- **Prove:** `canfail prove` planted all 45 candidate mutations in `src/pricing.ts` (`--bugs all`, seed 1) and the suite caught all 45. The source file was restored afterward; `git status` shows only the new test file.

The expected values come from `REQUIREMENTS.md`, worked out by hand rather than copied from the output. The tests cover:
- the basic total (subtotal, tax, shipping);
- the 10% discount at exactly 100 and just below;
- the 20% discount at exactly 500 and just below;
- SAVE5 applied after the percentage discount, and clamped at zero;
- tax-exempt orders;
- the free-shipping threshold at exactly 50 and just below;
- digital-only orders (no shipping) and mixed orders (shipping applies);
- `RangeError` for quantities of 0, -1, and 1.5.

I put the file next to the module in `src/` because vitest finds `*.test.ts` there by default. The repo had no existing tests, so there was no convention to match. I did not commit anything.
